{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790292878,"nonce":"X4K/Dx77+0xfRM1ZWJ2QSP7Goww=","title":"Lua: string.dump is missing","message":"string.dump is nil, so the official suite stops where it first dumps a function: db.lua:55 (load(string.dump(load(\"print(10)\"), true))) and calls.lua:331. lua5.4 returns the function's binary chunk, which load then accepts in mode 'b'. A zylua function has no bytecode; a dump would need a serialized form of the chunk (its source and the function's position in it would do for load's purposes), and load would need to take it back. Found while running the debug library package (L-debug-library).","files":null}]}